 "title": "Breathy Acid Pad",
 "category": "Pads and atmospheres",
 "text": "Sound: a soft, airy, slowly swirling pad, the hazy backdrop behind acid and trance vocals: chords that fade in with a breath of noise.\n\nHow it's built: a pulse wave whose width is swept by a slow LFO (PWM, the swirl), with a little white noise mixed in (the breath); a gentle Ladder filter; a slow attack and long release; Chorus (Ensemble) and a large Reverb. Six voices.\n\nPlay: slow chords.\n\nTweak: the envelope's ATTACK and RELEASE, the noise level (mixer 2), the LFO's RATE, the filter's CUTOFF.",
